word ladder builder
==================

Write a function:

    def word_ladder_builder(start: str, end: str, wordlist: list[str]) -> int

A ladder is a sequence of words in which each step changes exactly one
letter, and every word after the first must come from the wordlist. Return
the LENGTH of the shortest ladder from start to end, counting both
endpoints (start -> hot -> dot has length 3). If end is not in the
wordlist, or no ladder exists, return 0.

Examples:
    word_ladder_builder("hit", "cog", ["hot", "dot", "dog", "lot", "log", "cog"]) -> 5
    word_ladder_builder("hit", "cog", ["hot", "dot", "dog", "lot", "log"]) -> 0
    word_ladder_builder("a", "c", ["a", "b", "c"]) -> 2
    word_ladder_builder("hot", "dog", ["hot", "dog"]) -> 0
    word_ladder_builder("hot", "hot", ["hot"]) -> 1
